### Sample requests (IntelliJ HTTP client / VS Code REST Client). Run ./run.sh and ./seed.sh first.
@proxy = http://localhost:8000
@admin = admin
@adminPassword = admin-dev-password

### --- Admin API (HTTP Basic) ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Supported strategies and time periods
GET {{proxy}}/admin/api/policies/strategies
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### MUC3: the pre-created default policy
GET {{proxy}}/admin/api/policies/default
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### MUC4: create a policy
POST {{proxy}}/admin/api/policies
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "burst-5-per-second", "rate_limiting_strategy": "token-bucket", "number_of_requests": 5, "time_period": "second"}

### MUC4: list policies (filter + pagination)
GET {{proxy}}/admin/api/policies?name=minute&page=0&size=10
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### MUC1.4: fetch resources from the target's OpenAPI document
POST {{proxy}}/admin/api/resources/sync
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### Resources (filters: path, method, io_type, resource_group_id)
GET {{proxy}}/admin/api/resources?io_type=write&size=50
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### Resource groups
GET {{proxy}}/admin/api/resource-groups
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### MUC1.1: consumer groups are created with their first consumers (fails with 409 after seed.sh)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/api/consumer-groups
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"group_name": "premium", "consumer_ids": ["premium-user-9"]}

### MUC1.2: create a consumer in a group (use an id from GET /admin/api/consumer-groups)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/api/consumers
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"consumer_id": "regular-user-9", "consumer_group_id": 2}

### MUC2: assignments of one consumer group
GET {{proxy}}/admin/api/consumer-groups-policies?consumer_group_id=2
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### MUC1.5: assign a policy to a resource group (relationship_type: resource | resource_group)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/api/consumer-groups-policies
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"consumer_group_id": 3, "relationship_type": "resource_group", "policy_id": 2, "resource_id": 2}

### Development token for a consumer
POST {{proxy}}/admin/api/tokens
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"consumer_id": "free-user-1"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### Evict the rule cache on every instance
DELETE {{proxy}}/admin/api/cache
Authorization: Basic {{admin}} {{adminPassword}}

### --- Consumer traffic (Bearer token) -----------------------------------------------------

### CUC1: proxied exactly like the target API; repeat 11 times to get HTTP 429
GET {{proxy}}/orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Writes of the free tier: token bucket, 3 per minute
POST {{proxy}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"item": "book"}

### Default policy (nothing assigned for free tier on /users)
GET {{proxy}}/users/42
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Missing token -> 401 JSON
GET {{proxy}}/carts
